<title>MALAYSIA: Country Heights plans 3-for-5 bonus.</title>
<headline>Country Heights plans 3-for-5 bonus.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian property developer Country Heights Bhd said it was planning a bonus issue in the ratio of three shares for every five held.</p>
<p>The bonus issue will capitalise 135 million ringgit from the company's reserves and share premium account at one ringgit per share, the company said in a statement to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>It said the bonus issue will increase the company's paid up share capital and better reflect the current size of its operations.</p>
<p>&quot;(It) is expected to improve the liquidity of CHHB shares in the market,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>However, the issue has to be cleared by the Securities Commission and the company's shareholders, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
</text>
